      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span><span class=\"time\">15 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip ok\">Easy</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Simulation</span><span class=\"chip accent\">DP</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Combinatorics</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/pascals-triangle/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 118</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Pascal's Triangle</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Build the first numRows rows. Every row starts and ends with 1, and every inner entry is the sum of the two entries above it: <code>row[i][j] = row[i-1][j-1] + row[i-1][j]</code>. O(numRows²) time, which is exactly the size of the output. Entry j of row i is also the binomial coefficient C(i, j), which is what the follow-ups ask about.</p>\n"
  },
